  "summary": "Postinstall dependency-manager fetches and executes remote install script from third-party GitHub repo",
  "details": "scripts/dependency-manager.js runs execSync('curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rtk-ai/rtk/refs/heads/master/install.sh...'), fetching and executing a shell script from a mutable branch (refs/heads/master) of an unrelated third-party GitHub repository (rtk-ai/rtk) at install time. The script also contacts https://www.rtk-ai.app and https://api.github.com, reads os.homedir() and process.platform, and shells out via child_process. Because the fetched install.sh is retrieved from a mutable branch with no pinning, hash check, or signature verification, whoever controls that repository can substitute arbitrary code that executes on the installer's machine on every install. The package name (@leejungkiin/awkit) is unrelated to rtk-ai, so the fetch pulls third-party code, not first-party publisher content. Additional shipped files (bin/awk.js, scripts/model-manager.js) also combine child_process with hardcoded HTTP endpoints.",
